HTTPTunnelPort 127.0.0.1:8118
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:53530
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
CookieAuthentication 1
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1
SocksPolicy reject *

GeoIPFile data/geoip
GeoIPv6File data/geoipv6

CircuitPadding 0
ConnectionPadding 0
UseMicrodescriptors 1
HardwareAcceleration 1

DormantOnFirstStartup 0
DormantCanceledByStartup 1
LearnCircuitBuildTimeout 1
MaxCircuitDirtiness 1800
NumEntryGuards 10
NumDirectoryGuards 6
KeepalivePeriod 3600
ClientUseIPv6 1

ClientBootstrapConsensusAuthorityDownloadInitialDelay 0
ClientBootstrapConsensusFallbackDownloadInitialDelay 0
ClientBootstrapConsensusAuthorityOnlyDownloadInitialDelay 0
ClientBootstrapConsensusMaxInProgressTries 10

FetchDirInfoEarly 1
FetchDirInfoExtraEarly 1

PathsNeededToBuildCircuits 0.25

ClientTransportPlugin webtunnel exec Transport/webtunnel.exe
ClientTransportPlugin obfs4 exec Transport/obfs4proxy.exe
ClientTransportPlugin snowflake exec Transport/snowflake-client.exe

DataDirectory data
DisableDebuggerAttachment 1
AvoidDiskWrites 1
SafeLogging 1

ConfluxEnabled 1
ConfluxClientUX throughput

SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
# Dedicated keep-alive port expected by the conflux keep-alive logic.
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9052 NoIsolateSOCKSAuth

CircuitsAvailableTimeout 4320
CircuitStreamTimeout 60
CircuitBuildTimeout 40
NumPrimaryGuards 15
# KISTLite is the best scheduler available on Windows; Vanilla is only fallback.
Schedulers KIST,KISTLite,Vanilla
MaxClientCircuitsPending 256
CircuitPriorityHalflife 5
SocksTimeout 120

# Keep a small pool of ready conflux sets and spread streams across all of them
# (fewest-streams policy) instead of building 32 sets but only using the fastest
# handful. Leave the RTT percentage filter off so every prebuilt set carries
# user traffic, but skip clearly slow sets via ConfluxSetRttMax.
ConfluxNumSets 8
ConfluxNumLinkedSets 8
ConfluxNumLegs 3
ConfluxSetSelection 2
ConfluxSetRttPct 0
ConfluxSetRttMax 800
# With more than two legs per set (ConfluxNumLegs above), upstream's conflux
# scheduler wants cfx_drain_pct 100 so a leg can be switched away from as soon
# as its in-flight data drains; otherwise switching is blocked.
ConfluxDrainPct 100
# Keep the full prebuilt-set pool even though conflux Exits are a minority:
# by default tor builds a single prebuilt set when under 60% of Exits support
# conflux, which caps parallelism.
ConfluxLowExitThreshold 1
